<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; connect-src 'none'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'">
  <title>S121 — Windows code-slot promotion rehearsal</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  <script src="model.js" defer></script>
  <script src="app.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <p id="training-banner" class="banner">Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result</p>
  <h1>Windows code-slot promotion rehearsal</h1>
  <p>A-S121 · D-S121 · SC-S121 · one Kano S learning unit</p>
  <p>Rehearse preparation before a fictional promotion, then inspect client receipts.
    Declared configuration, HTTP 200, and a wished swap are not native or complete-journey evidence.</p>
  <section aria-labelledby="envelope-heading">
    <h2 id="envelope-heading">Fixed fictional envelope — DATA ONLY</h2>
    <p>Hosting label: App Service / Windows / code. SKU label: TEACH-SLOT-SKU (invented,
      not an Azure SKU or selection). Region: classroom-region. Slots: production and staging;
      both share the same fictional plan and reserved overlap headroom.</p>
    <p>Code: win-code-v1 → win-code-v2. Slot-specific setting: profile-store=shared-teaching-store.
      Warm-up declaration: WEBSITE_SWAP_WARMUP_PING_PATH=/ready/strict;
      WEBSITE_SWAP_WARMUP_PING_STATUSES=200. Readiness budget: 120 ms.
      Three getProfile → update → confirm journeys; 180 ms per whole journey,
      identity/state preserved, one committed effect each, zero duplicates.</p>
    <p>No identity, setting, slot, routing, configuration, or infrastructure is deployed.
      These are fixture labels and numbers, not recommendations or Azure observations.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="controls-heading">
    <h2 id="controls-heading">Operator actions</h2>
    <p>1. Configure a fixed case. 2. Inspect receipts. 3. Request a fictional promotion
      only if prepared. 4. Observe the fixed journey trace. Reset to try another case.</p>
    <form id="lesson-form" novalidate>
      <label for="fixture">Teaching case</label>
      <select id="fixture" name="fixture"></select>
      <label for="target">Fictional swap target</label>
      <select id="target" name="target">
        <option value="production">production — intended target</option>
        <option value="staging">staging — deliberate wrong-target case</option>
      </select>
      <label class="acknowledgement" for="synthetic-ack">
        <input id="synthetic-ack" name="synthetic-ack" type="checkbox">
        I understand this is a synthetic rehearsal, not a live operation.
      </label>
      <button id="configure" type="submit">1. Configure teaching case</button>
    </form>
    <div class="actions">
      <button id="inspect" type="button" disabled>2. Inspect preparation receipts</button>
      <button id="request-promotion" type="button" disabled>3. Request fictional promotion</button>
      <button id="observe" type="button" disabled>4. Observe fictional journeys</button>
      <button id="reset-lesson" type="button">Reset lesson</button>
    </div>
    <p id="input-error" role="alert" tabindex="-1" hidden></p>
    <p id="action-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Baseline restored. Choose a teaching case.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="result-heading">
    <h2 id="result-heading" tabindex="-1">Measured teaching result</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>Phase</dt><dd id="phase">baseline</dd>
      <dt>Declared configuration</dt><dd id="declared-configuration">Not configured</dd>
      <dt>Effective configuration receipt</dt><dd id="configuration-receipt">Not observed</dd>
      <dt>Desired routing</dt><dd id="desired-routing"></dd>
      <dt>Observed routing</dt><dd id="observed-routing"></dd>
      <dt>Educational verifier</dt><dd id="verification">PENDING</dd>
      <dt>User-transition classification</dt><dd id="classification">Not measured</dd>
      <dt>Attempted / successful / interrupted / unknown</dt><dd id="counts">0 / 0 / 0 / 0</dd>
      <dt>Transition fraction</dt><dd id="fraction">No transition sample</dd>
      <dt>Native claim</dt><dd id="native-claim">UNVERIFIED — no live Azure evidence</dd>
      <dt>Cleanup</dt><dd id="cleanup">Local memory only; no resources created</dd>
    </dl>
    <p>PASS means the expected teaching outcome was recognized, including a negative or unknown
      result. A safe abort has no migrated sample. An old-destination or unfinished journey
      is not a successful transition. No result here proves the source parent or five-nines goal.</p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table id="gate-table">
        <caption>Preparation gates: fictional expected versus measured receipts</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Gate</th><th scope="col">Expected</th><th scope="col">Measured DATA</th><th scope="col">Verdict</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody id="gates"></tbody>
      </table>
      <table id="journey-table">
        <caption>Started fictional journeys — failures and unknowns stay in the denominator</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Journey</th><th scope="col">Destination</th><th scope="col">Identity / state</th><th scope="col">Effects / duplicates</th><th scope="col">Whole-journey ms / HTTP</th><th scope="col">Outcome</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody id="journeys"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h3>Retained action history (this run; at most four accepted actions)</h3>
    <ol id="history"></ol>
    <p>Invalid actions preserve the last valid state and history. Reset explicitly clears this
      run, selections, and acknowledgement. Reload also starts a fresh in-memory rehearsal.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="native-heading">
    <h2 id="native-heading">What a native Windows claim would still need</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Separate authorization and an owned Windows code target, supporting SKU/slot limits,
        region, configuration, immutable versions, and shared-plan overlap capacity evidence.</li>
      <li>Target-specific effective settings, including slot-specific/non-swapped properties,
        plus strict warm-up path/status and dependency, authentication, state, and latency receipts.</li>
      <li>A real swap record with production as target and actual destination/version receipts,
        not desired traffic weights, an HTTP-only probe, or a requested operation.</li>
      <li>Finished representative journeys with identity/state, latency, committed effects,
        duplicate/missing effects, unknowns, routing-cookie clients, and former-worker outcomes.</li>
      <li>Native prerequisite acceptance, independent verifier/user-impact/cleanup evidence,
        and appropriately qualified statistical evidence for any reliability claim.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Documented Windows code swaps require a supporting plan, but this is not target
      qualification. Slots share compute; retaining an old slot does not prevent native
      swap worker recycling. A zero-traffic staging endpoint is not authorization.
      Linux/container native auto-swap exclusions are not borrowed as Windows proof.</p>
    <p>B-S121, C061/C064 and D-S121 remain unfulfilled. The production Node.js 24 / Express
      design is not validated by the Node.js 22 test tooling used for this lesson.</p>
  </section>
</main>
</body>
</html>
